.TH GARNISH 7 2026-11-04 garnish "garnish manual"
.SH NAME
garnish \- Linux applications from other distributions in lightweight VMs
.SH DESCRIPTION
garnish runs Linux applications from other distributions in small crosvm
virtual machines, with their windows on the host's Wayland desktop. Each
guest's Wayland applications reach the host through sommelier, so they open
as ordinary windows, and its installed applications show up in the host's
application menu. Guests are VMs, not containers: they can't see each
other, get no microphone unless allowed, and only share the host directory
they are given. Nothing runs as root, except the optional NAT helper.
.SH COMPONENTS
.SS On the host
.TP
.BR gerantd (1)
The session-bus daemon that starts and stops VMs.
.TP
.BR gerant (1)
Its command line client.
.TP
.BR gerant\-net (8)
The setuid helper that creates network devices for VMs with
.BR Mode=nat .
.TP
.BR salle (1)
A GTK application to create, edit, start and stop VMs.
.TP
.BR carte (1)
Puts the guests' applications in the host's menu.
.TP
.BR sonnette (1)
Shows the guests' notifications on the host.
.TP
.BR videur (1)
Controls which way a guest's clipboard goes.
.SS In the guest
.TP
.BR carte\-agent (1)
Serves the guest's applications to
.BR carte .
.TP
.BR sonnette\-agent (1)
The guest's notification server, which forwards to
.BR sonnette .
.TP
.B sommelier
Shows the guest's Wayland windows on the host.
.TP
.B gerant\-ready.service
Tells
.B gerantd
when the guest has booted.
.SS Configuration
.TP
.BR garnish\-vm.conf (5)
One file per VM.
.TP
.BR gerantd.conf (5)
vsock CIDs, DNS and the stop timeout.
.TP
.BR garnish\-network.conf (5)
The NAT VMs' networks, for all users.
.SH VSOCK PORTS
.TP
.B 8890
.BR carte\-agent ,
in the guest.
.TP
.B 8891
Boot notifications, on the host.
.TP
.B 8892
.BR sonnette\-agent ,
in the guest.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ mkdir \-p ~/.config/garnish/vms
$ cp /usr/share/doc/gerant/examples/debian.conf ~/.config/garnish/vms/
$ $EDITOR ~/.config/garnish/vms/debian.conf    # set Image=
$ gerant start debian
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crosvm (1),
.BR passt (1)
.PP
.UR https://github.com/jonnsl/garnish
.UE
